What:		/sys/bus/hid/drivers/hid-apple-mtp-haptic/<dev>/click_strength
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Strengths at which the actuator firmware plays its own click
		waveforms while the actuator is device-controlled, written and
		read as <press>,<release>, 1-255 each. They are used over the
		device tree's apple,click-strength, and written again after
		every resume.

		0,0, the default, uses the device tree's values, or the
		firmware's own when there are none; a strength set earlier is
		then taken back to the firmware's boot value. A pair with only
		one half 0 is refused.

		Reading returns the pair last written here, not the device
		tree's values.
